I walk over to the friendly shop assistant.
I smile and show her the blue shirt and my receipt.
"Hi, I bought this shirt on Saturday," I say.
"But unfortunately, it is too small."
"Can I exchange it for a larger size?"
"Yes, of course you can," the assistant answers.
"Which size do you need?"
"I need a large instead of a medium," I explain.
"One moment," the assistant says.
She walks over to the shelves with the blue shirts.
She quickly finds the right size and comes back.
"Here is a large," she says with a smile.
"Do you want to try it on first?"
"Yes please," I reply happily.
"The fitting rooms are right over there to the right," she tells me.
"Thank you very much for the help," I say and take the new shirt.
Now I can see if the larger shirt is better.
